---
/**
 * Privacy Policy.
 *
 * Written against the schema rather than from a template: every field named in
 * section 2 exists on `person`, `person_interest`, `person_link`,
 * `consent_record` or `notification`, and nothing is listed that we do not
 * actually store. When a column is added, this page is part of the change.
 *
 * The structure is the conventional one — controller, categories, purposes,
 * recipients, retention, rights, grievance — because a person comparing this
 * against another organisation's notice should be able to find the same
 * section in the same place.
 */
import Doc from '../layouts/Doc.astro';
import { POLICY_LABEL, POLICY_UPDATED } from '../lib/policy';
---

<Doc
	title="Privacy Policy — The Itti Foundation"
	description="How The Itti Foundation collects, uses, shares and retains personal data, and the rights you have over it."
	eyebrow="Privacy Policy"
	heading="Privacy Policy"
	lede="What we collect, why we collect it, who else sees it, how long we keep it, and what you can require of us."
	version={POLICY_LABEL}
	updated={POLICY_UPDATED}
>
	<section class="doc__section">
		<h2 class="doc__h">1. Scope and controller</h2>
		<div class="doc__body">
			<p>
				This policy applies to <code>itti.org.in</code> and to the registry behind it. The
				data fiduciary is <strong>Itti&rsquo;s Skill School Foundation</strong>, a Section
				8 not-for-profit company incorporated in India and operating as The Itti
				Foundation.
			</p>
			<p>
				It is written under India&rsquo;s Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023. Where
				that Act says <em>data principal</em>, this policy says <em>you</em>; where it says{' '}
				<em>data fiduciary</em>, it says <em>we</em>.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="doc__section">
		<h2 class="doc__h">2. Personal data we collect</h2>
		<div class="doc__body">
			<p><strong>2.1 Information you provide when registering.</strong></p>
			<dl class="doc__list">
				<dt>Identity</dt>
				<dd>
					Full name; your stated role (patient or beneficiary, caregiver or family member,
					volunteer or supporter, member); date of birth, if given; gender, including a
					self-described value where you choose that option.
				</dd>
				<dt>Contact</dt>
				<dd>
					Email address and telephone number. At least one is required; both are optional
					individually. We record whether each has been verified.
				</dd>
				<dt>Location</dt>
				<dd>City and, if given, six-digit PIN code. We do not collect a street address.</dd>
				<dt>Preferences</dt>
				<dd>
					Preferred language; which of our three areas of work you wish to be connected
					with; and separate permissions for contact by WhatsApp, SMS and email.
				</dd>
				<dt>Guardian details</dt>
				<dd>
					Where the registrant is under 18: the name, and the email address or telephone
					number, of a parent or guardian.
				</dd>
				<dt>Source</dt>
				<dd>
					How you heard of us, and the name of a referrer where you supply one.
				</dd>
			</dl>

			<p><strong>2.2 Information you add to your account.</strong></p>
			<dl class="doc__list">
				<dt>Profile text</dt>
				<dd>
					A short biography in your own words, up to 600 characters. It is optional and
					is shown only to you, on your account page.
				</dd>
				<dt>Links</dt>
				<dd>
					Handles or addresses you choose to add for Instagram, Facebook, YouTube,
					LinkedIn, a website, or an additional email address. These are self-asserted: we
					do not verify that an account belongs to you, and we do not access any of them.
				</dd>
				<dt>Display preference</dt>
				<dd>The colour you select for your account page.</dd>
			</dl>

			<p><strong>2.3 Information generated by your use of the site.</strong></p>
			<dl class="doc__list">
				<dt>Authentication</dt>
				<dd>
					When you sign in we create an authentication record holding your email address
					and the times you signed in. We do not set, store or ask for a password.
				</dd>
				<dt>Campaign parameters</dt>
				<dd>
					If you arrive by a tagged link, the campaign parameters in that link (commonly{' '}
					<code>utm_source</code>, <code>utm_medium</code>, <code>utm_campaign</code>) are
					recorded with your registration.
				</dd>
				<dt>Consent records</dt>
				<dd>
					Each permission you grant or withdraw, with its date and the version of this
					policy in force at the time. These are append-only: a withdrawal is a new entry,
					never a deletion.
				</dd>
				<dt>Correspondence</dt>
				<dd>
					A record of the messages we have sent you, their delivery status, and the
					details included in them.
				</dd>
			</dl>

			<p><strong>2.4 What we do not collect.</strong></p>
			<p>
				We do not use analytics, advertising or tracking services. We do not profile you,
				and no decision affecting you is made by automated means. We do not collect health
				information through this website.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="doc__section">
		<h2 class="doc__h">3. Purposes and lawful basis</h2>
		<div class="doc__body">
			<p>
				Under the DPDP Act we process personal data on the basis of your consent, given at
				registration and withdrawable at any time.
			</p>
			<dl class="doc__list">
				<dt>To reach you</dt>
				<dd>
					To acknowledge your registration and to contact you about the work you asked to
					be connected with, by the channels you permitted.
				</dd>
				<dt>To direct you correctly</dt>
				<dd>
					Your role, stated areas of interest and location determine which part of the
					Foundation responds to you.
				</dd>
				<dt>To obtain guardian consent</dt>
				<dd>
					Where a registrant is under 18, to notify the parent or guardian named and to
					obtain their agreement before acting on the registration.
				</dd>
				<dt>To operate your account</dt>
				<dd>To authenticate you and to display the record we hold about you.</dd>
				<dt>To understand our reach</dt>
				<dd>
					Aggregate counts by city, area of interest and referral source, used to plan
					where the Foundation works. This does not identify individuals.
				</dd>
				<dt>To meet legal obligations</dt>
				<dd>To retain consent records and to respond to lawful requests.</dd>
			</dl>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="doc__section">
		<h2 class="doc__h">4. Consent, and how to withdraw it</h2>
		<div class="doc__body">
			<p>
				Permission for WhatsApp, SMS and email is asked for separately and recorded
				separately. You may change any of them at any time on your account page, or by
				writing to us; the change takes effect on receipt and we record it.
			</p>
			<p>
				Withdrawing consent does not affect anything done while it was in force, and does
				not by itself erase your record. To have the record removed, see section 9.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="doc__section">
		<h2 class="doc__h">5. Children</h2>
		<div class="doc__body">
			<p>
				The DPDP Act treats anyone under 18 as a child and requires verifiable consent from
				a parent or lawful guardian. A registration giving a date of birth under 18 cannot
				be completed without guardian details; the registry refuses it.
			</p>
			<p>
				We write to the guardian at the address given and do not act on the registration
				until they agree. We do not use a child&rsquo;s data for tracking, advertising or
				behavioural monitoring of any kind.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="doc__section">
		<h2 class="doc__h">6. Recipients and processors</h2>
		<div class="doc__body">
			<p>
				We do not sell personal data, and we do not share it for anyone else&rsquo;s
				marketing. It is disclosed only to the service providers below, who process it on
				our instructions and for no purpose of their own.
			</p>
			<dl class="doc__list">
				<dt>Supabase</dt>
				<dd>
					Database, authentication and server functions. Your data is held in the Mumbai
					region.
				</dd>
				<dt>Cloudflare</dt>
				<dd>
					Hosting, content delivery and DNS for this website. Cloudflare processes the
					network requests your browser makes, including your IP address, in order to
					serve pages.
				</dd>
				<dt>Resend</dt>
				<dd>Delivery of automated email, including sign-in links and acknowledgements.</dd>
				<dt>Zoho</dt>
				<dd>
					Our own mailboxes. Correspondence you send to an <code>@itti.org.in</code>{' '}
					address is held there.
				</dd>
				<dt>India Post PIN directory</dt>
				<dd>
					If you enter a PIN code, your browser queries a public postal lookup
					(<code>api.postalpincode.in</code>) to name the district. Only the PIN code is
					sent, and it is not accompanied by anything identifying you.
				</dd>
			</dl>
			<p>
				We may also disclose personal data where required by law, or to establish or defend
				a legal claim.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="doc__section">
		<h2 class="doc__h">7. Storage and transfers</h2>
		<div class="doc__body">
			<p>
				The registry is hosted in India, in Supabase&rsquo;s Mumbai region. Our email
				providers and content delivery network operate globally and may process data
				outside India in the course of delivering a message or a page. We use providers
				that offer contractual protections for such transfers.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="doc__section">
		<h2 class="doc__h">8. Retention</h2>
		<div class="doc__body">
			<dl class="doc__list">
				<dt>Your registration and account</dt>
				<dd>
					Kept while you remain in contact with the Foundation, and erased on request.
				</dd>
				<dt>Consent records</dt>
				<dd>
					Kept for the life of the registration and for three years afterwards, because
					they are the evidence of what you agreed to and when.
				</dd>
				<dt>Correspondence records</dt>
				<dd>Kept for two years from the date of sending.</dd>
			</dl>
			<p>
				Where a retention period has passed, data is deleted or irreversibly aggregated so
				that it no longer identifies anyone.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="doc__section">
		<h2 class="doc__h">9. Your rights</h2>
		<div class="doc__body">
			<p>Under the DPDP Act you have the right to:</p>
			<dl class="doc__list">
				<dt>Access</dt>
				<dd>
					Obtain confirmation of what we hold about you and a summary of how it is
					processed. Your account page shows this in full and at any time.
				</dd>
				<dt>Correction and completion</dt>
				<dd>
					Have inaccurate data corrected and incomplete data completed. Most fields can be
					edited directly on your account page.
				</dd>
				<dt>Erasure</dt>
				<dd>
					Require deletion of your personal data, except where we must retain it to meet a
					legal obligation.
				</dd>
				<dt>Grievance redressal</dt>
				<dd>Raise a complaint with us, and receive a response.</dd>
				<dt>Nomination</dt>
				<dd>
					Nominate another individual to exercise these rights on your behalf in the event
					of your death or incapacity.
				</dd>
			</dl>
			<p>
				To exercise any of these, write to{' '}
				<a class="doc__link" href="mailto:hello@itti.org.in">hello@itti.org.in</a>. We
				respond within five working days and complete requests within thirty days.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="doc__section">
		<h2 class="doc__h">10. Security</h2>
		<div class="doc__body">
			<p>
				Access to the registry is restricted at the database level: a signed-in person can
				read and amend their own record and no other. Staff access is limited to those who
				need it. The site is served only over HTTPS and enforces a content security policy.
			</p>
			<p>
				No system is immune to compromise. In the event of a personal data breach we will
				notify the Data Protection Board of India and every affected person, as the Act
				requires.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="doc__section">
		<h2 class="doc__h">11. Cookies and browser storage</h2>
		<div class="doc__body">
			<p>
				<strong>We set no advertising or analytics cookies.</strong> The site uses browser
				storage for two strictly functional purposes:
			</p>
			<dl class="doc__list">
				<dt>Your session</dt>
				<dd>
					When you sign in, an authentication token is stored in your browser so that you
					remain signed in. Signing out removes it.
				</dd>
				<dt>Your display name and colour</dt>
				<dd>
					Your first name and chosen colour are stored locally so the site can show them
					without querying the registry on every page. They never leave your device.
				</dd>
			</dl>
			<p>Clearing your browser&rsquo;s site data removes both and signs you out.</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="doc__section">
		<h2 class="doc__h">12. Changes to this policy</h2>
		<div class="doc__body">
			<p>
				This policy carries a version number and a date, both shown at the head of this
				page. When it changes materially we update both and record the version in force
				against each consent we hold, so that it is always possible to establish which
				terms you agreed to.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="doc__section">
		<h2 class="doc__h">13. Contact and grievances</h2>
		<div class="doc__body">
			<p>
				<strong>Grievance Officer:</strong> Anuja Bali, The Itti Foundation.<br />
				<strong>Email:</strong>{' '}
				<a class="doc__link" href="mailto:hello@itti.org.in">hello@itti.org.in</a><br />
				<strong>Telephone:</strong>{' '}
				<a class="doc__link" href="tel:+918928263631">+91 89282 63631</a>
			</p>
			<p>
				If you are not satisfied with our response, you may complain to the Data Protection
				Board of India.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>
</Doc>
